# Windows checks out with core.autocrlf on by default, and several checks locate
# blocks in the frontend sources with literal \n needles — styles.indexOf(
# '.topbar-actions {\n  display: grid') and friends. A CRLF working tree turns
# those into -1, so the check slices an empty string and asserts against '',
# which reads as a UI regression rather than as a line-ending difference.
#
# Nothing in this repository is generated on a platform that needs CRLF, so the
# simplest correct answer is to never translate.
* -text
